% A power wheelchair for a beneficiary about whom nothing says a scooter
% would not do: the answer is conditional on that finding.
scenario scooter_not_ruled_out is:
    claim 1 is for the power wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the power wheelchair is "K0823".
    the power wheelchair is furnished to Cy.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair not self propellable about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding power wheelchair can be safely operated about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates power wheelchair about Cy is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding power wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use power wheelchair at home about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the weight of Cy is 180 pounds.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding scooter ruled out about Cy is established"].

% The Council finds the record does not show that a cane or walker would not
% do: the claim is not reasonable and necessary.
scenario walking_aids_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the power wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the power wheelchair is "K0823".
    the power wheelchair is furnished to Dee.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Dee is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the record shows the beneficiary ambulating with a walker".
    the finding manual wheelchair not self propellable about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding scooter ruled out about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding power wheelchair can be safely operated about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates power wheelchair about Dee is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding power wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use power wheelchair at home about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the weight of Dee is 180 pounds.
    rn expects answers [].

% Weight: a 320-pound beneficiary is outside the standard class (K0823) and
% inside the heavy-duty class (K0824).
scenario weight_class is:
    claim 1 is for the standard chair.
    the HCPCS code of the standard chair is "K0823".
    the standard chair is furnished to Eve.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    claim 2 is for the heavy duty chair.
    the HCPCS code of the heavy duty chair is "K0824".
    the heavy duty chair is furnished to Eve.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair not self propellable about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding scooter ruled out about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding power wheelchair can be safely operated about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates power wheelchair about Eve is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding power wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use power wheelchair at home about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the weight of Eve is 320 pounds.
    rn expects answers ["claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A Group 3 single power option chair (K0856): a neurological diagnosis, a
% power tilt seating system, the specialty evaluation and the ATP.
scenario group_3_single_power is:
    claim 1 is for the rehab chair.
    the HCPCS code of the rehab chair is "K0856".
    the rehab chair is furnished to Fay.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair not self propellable about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding scooter ruled out about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding power wheelchair can be safely operated about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates power wheelchair about Fay is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding power wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use power wheelchair at home about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding qualifying group 3 diagnosis about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "multiple sclerosis".
    the finding single power option justified about Fay is established, according to the physical therapist.
    Fay had a specialty evaluation by a licensed medical professional with no financial relationship with the supplier for the rehab chair.
    a RESNA certified assistive technology professional employed by the supplier was directly involved in the selection of the rehab chair.
    the weight of Fay is 150 pounds.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

